1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,421
In 1861, Harriet Colfax took charge of

2
00:00:03,431 --> 00:00:04,927
Michigan City's lighthouse.

3
00:00:05,157 --> 00:00:07,561
She kept the light burning for 43 years.

4
00:00:08,011 --> 00:00:09,553
She lived in the lighthouse with her

5
00:00:09,563 --> 00:00:11,559
lifelong companion, Ann Hartwell.

6
00:00:11,959 --> 00:00:13,961
Every night of the shipping season, she

7
00:00:13,971 --> 00:00:15,458
lit the lights after sunset.

8
00:00:15,858 --> 00:00:19,344
After 1871, she also walked a long, raised

9
00:00:19,354 --> 00:00:21,818
walkway out the pier to a second light,

10
00:00:21,828 --> 00:00:23,452
even when ice coated the walk.

11
00:00:23,902 --> 00:00:27,512
In 1873, she wrote in her log: A terrible

12
00:00:27,522 --> 00:00:28,434
hurricane tonight.

13
00:00:28,884 --> 00:00:32,015
Harriet retired in 1904, at about 80.

14
00:00:32,245 --> 00:00:33,614
She died the next spring.

15
00:00:34,064 --> 00:00:36,380
Her 1858 lighthouse still stands.

16
00:00:36,610 --> 00:00:40,044
It's been a museum since 1973, open April

17
00:00:40,054 --> 00:00:40,908
through October.

18
00:00:41,408 --> 00:00:43,451
Comment your town, and it could be next.

